{%- comment -%}
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PRODUCT BADGES COMPONENT
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This component is used in product listing and product page to render the badges of a given product

********************************************
Supported variables
********************************************

* product: the product to render the badges
* variant: the specific variant to show the badge from
* context: can be "product" or "card"
* direction: can be "column" or "row". If none is passed, it defaults to "row"
* alignment: can be "start", "center" or "end" (default to start)
* vertical_text: if true, badges text are shown vertically
* show_custom_badge: if set to true, the custom badge from metafield is shown
* show_sold_out_badge: if set to true, the sold out badge is shown
* show_discount_badge: if set to true, the discount badge is shown
* class: an extra list of classes being applied to the badge list container
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- assign variant = variant | default: product.selected_or_first_available_variant -%}

{%- comment -%}
  On search results, the variant that textually matched the query (e.g. a sold-out numbered
  edition) can be resolved as "selected" even with no ?variant= URL param, making an in-stock
  product show a false "Sold out" badge. Fall back to an available SYSTEM ASSIGNED (AUTO)
  variant that matches on every other option (e.g. framing style, when present) when that
  happens. Works for both single-option (edition-only) and multi-option (framing + edition)
  products. No-op if the variant passed in is already available or no matching fallback
  exists.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  if variant.available == false
    assign requested_options = variant.options
    assign available_variants = product.variants | where: 'available', true
    for v in available_variants
      assign is_match = true
      for opt_val in v.options
        assign idx = forloop.index0
        assign requested_val = requested_options[idx]
        if opt_val != requested_val and opt_val != 'SYSTEM ASSIGNED (AUTO)'
          assign is_match = false
        endif
      endfor
      if is_match and v.title contains 'SYSTEM ASSIGNED (AUTO)'
        assign variant = v
        break
      endif
    endfor
  endif
-%}

{%- capture badges -%}
  {%- if show_custom_badge -%}
    {%- for custom_badge in product.metafields.custom.badges.value -%}
      <span class="badge badge--custom badge--{{ custom_badge | handle }} {% if vertical_text %}vertical-text{% endif %}">{{ custom_badge }}</span>
    {%- endfor -%}
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- comment -%}
    On a card (search results, collection grids), there's no interactive variant picker, so
    "Sold out" should reflect whether the PRODUCT has anything purchasable at all
    (product.available), not just whichever variant search happened to resolve as "selected".
    On the actual product page, keep reflecting the specific variant currently shown, since a
    customer who manually picks a genuinely sold-out edition should see accurate feedback.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- liquid
    assign is_sold_out = false
    if context == 'card'
      unless product.available
        assign is_sold_out = true
      endunless
    else
      unless variant.available
        assign is_sold_out = true
      endunless
    endif
  -%}
  {%- if show_sold_out_badge and is_sold_out -%}
    <sold-out-badge {% if form_id != blank %}form="{{ form_id }}"{% endif %} class="badge badge--sold-out {% if vertical_text %}vertical-text{% endif %}">
      {{- 'product.general.sold_out_badge' | t -}}
    </sold-out-badge>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- if show_discount_badge -%}
    {%- liquid
      assign show_on_sale_badge = false

      if context == 'product'
        if variant.compare_at_price > variant.price
          assign show_on_sale_badge = true
        endif
      elsif context == 'card'
        if product.compare_at_price > product.price
          assign show_on_sale_badge = true
        endif
      endif
    -%}

    {%- if product.compare_at_price > product.price -%}
      {%- if settings.product_card_discount_mode == 'percentage' -%}
        {%- assign savings = variant.compare_at_price | minus: variant.price | times: 100.0 | divided_by: variant.compare_at_price | round | append: '%' -%}
      {%- else -%}
        {%- capture savings -%}{{ variant.compare_at_price | minus: variant.price | money }}{%- endcapture -%}
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if show_on_sale_badge -%}
        <on-sale-badge class="badge badge--on-sale {% if vertical_text %}vertical-text{% endif %}">
          {%- liquid
            if context == 'product'
              echo 'product.general.discount_badge_html' | t: savings: savings
            elsif context == 'card'
              if product.compare_at_price_varies or variant.compare_at_price == blank
                echo 'product.general.on_sale_badge' | t
              else
                echo 'product.general.discount_badge_html' | t: savings: savings
              endif
            endif
          -%}
        </on-sale-badge>
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endcapture -%}

{%- if badges != blank -%}
  <badge-list class="badge-list {% unless vertical_text %}badge-list--{{ direction | default: 'row' }}{% endunless %} {% if alignment %}{% if direction == 'column' %}align-{{ alignment }}{% else %}justify-{{ alignment }}{% endif %}{% endif %} {{ class }}">
    {{- badges -}}
  </badge-list>
{%- endif -%}